{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:58:12.359474Z","id":"9b9f8d251fddf878ac68e1943e22942251149f6f835962cbce5de66b441f9331","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/home.ts passes {x, y, w, h} from the page unchanged and HomeHost._rect builds a Rect from it. The frame's offset in the shell and the WebView's place on screen are not applied, so an anchored menu would be misplaced wherever the frame does not start at the screen's top left. Launcher's own HomeActions ignores the anchor (a bottom sheet). Whoever implements HomeActions.menu for the home route (plan Task 3) must map it, as host_protocol.dart's attestation maps pointer positions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":352},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"89575e5821e693c40b8b51b085c7a14e64a879dc2d6913be55f1d7028971cf0a"},"summary":"home.menu's rect is taken as Flutter logical pixels as given: CSS pixels in the page's frame, not mapped to the screen","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:58:12.359574Z","id":"a891774fd391ab5ce1b972804caeea6a888e0b7e41bff75143a11b8a5201c67b","body":{"detail":"No daemon route serves AppIcons' cached icons under the home app's origin; a data URL needs none and no cross-app read grant. It relies on the artifact CSP leaving img-src open (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs sets none) and grows apps() answers and every apps event by each icon's size.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":389},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"beafba81f576197bfca659cc09143bde8c4ef47c501c4efff9fdace12c434036"},"summary":"apps() gives an app's own icon as a data:image/svg+xml URL of the cleaned SVG, not a daemon-served URL as spec 2026-10-16 section 2 says","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:25:17.928487Z","id":"a47614ec7aae77343e9af4f3d78cdce1e641cd2a7a5a64bfec9c0094d8af5c13","body":{"detail":"ensureHomeApp installs through Installer.install, which writes the lineage entry with role installed and fromBundle: !mine (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:195-204); the home bundle is signed by its release key, never this install's, so mine is false. lib/app.dart passes fromBundleOf(_lineages) to the agent loop. Whether the home app, which the person changes by commenting, should be treated as code from a bundle is for plan Tasks 6 and 7 to settle.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"6d33ffada4a2495fed685ccbeec3b3dd77b78805eb8be9abcb38e149cd7999ee"},"summary":"The installed home app is recorded fromBundle: true, so the agent changes it under the bundle isolation rules (fromBundleOf), as any app installed from a file","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:25:17.928714Z","id":"3c16c72b617f5a0b2bddd2dcb8222723f065988a81170877b4899432d3d2306b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: AppScreen._onScreen (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart) moves home.menu's rect by the page view's place in the window (the surface widget's localToGlobal) before HomeHost.call builds the Rect. In app mode the shell's content frame starts at the WebView's top left (macOS integration run: the home app's grid drawn from the WebView's 0,0). flutter test test/home/home_route_test.dart: 'a menu rect from the page is moved onto the screen' passes (rect {x:5,y:100} on a view at (10,40) reaches HomeActions.menu as Rect.fromLTWH(15, 140, 60, 70)); +7 All tests passed.","supersedes":"9b9f8d251fddf878ac68e1943e22942251149f6f835962cbce5de66b441f9331","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:33:46.084271Z","id":"4d47246a3f92bf1608f37b8eb15377ce7e749ae87655731cd818f409439ec90a","body":{"detail":"If HomeSettings.save throws, _installHome (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:894-898) returns without settingsChanged, yet host.settings.homeAppId now holds the new ID, so the next HomeRoute rebuild for any other reason switches to the home app while home.json does not record it (the next launch adopts it by lineage).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"bc5003c9d1387fdbb68ae8e26d283a5e0c883370b52cc32099cc3ff97b0e4d56"},"suggested_fix":"Save a copy first, or restore the previous ID on failure.","summary":"ensureHomeApp sets settings.homeAppId before save; a failed save leaves the ID in memory, contrary to its doc 'with settings unchanged'","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:35:57.495649Z","id":"419b2696baf76ee0790f72ce4868a410d4eb193dbec32ef24bca9acaa8c00606","body":{"detail":"UpdateSheet in its modified form has only Keep mine and Update, but showBundleSheet is dismissible, so a null answer is possible. Asking again on the next start is the chosen reading of 'asks once per release' in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-home-screen-app-design.md section 5; treating a dismissal as Keep mine is the other.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"478e66199588ae9c9a8d0cfff3eb963ba9143f7fa3eabbc0d45b79a801452ab6"},"summary":"Closing the update sheet without answering (back, or the barrier) returns HomeUpdateResult.none and the same release asks again at the next start; only Keep mine stops the asking","tags":["home-app","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:47:28.557047Z","id":"25d12051d1e7edb4a0c56e63ca59c49f35a4a8311d8ddbd3ddf2d185d63b37f5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"419b2696baf76ee0790f72ce4868a410d4eb193dbec32ef24bca9acaa8c00606","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-16): closing the update sheet without answering asks again at the next start; keep the current behaviour.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:33.759726Z","id":"fcec3148dbed4924ad3a3c57786ac0b3b9a16baf639aba209356d0b74363b86d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: ensureHomeApp restores the previous homeAppId when save throws. Evidence: flutter test test/home/home_install_test.dart 'a home.json that cannot be written leaves the settings in memory unchanged' passes.","supersedes":"4d47246a3f92bf1608f37b8eb15377ce7e749ae87655731cd818f409439ec90a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:54.624167Z","id":"2be1402a9b0f7fcf0b83be6c7e6b596cb9fec8e4e45adb64b2e15f655cd7f452","body":{"detail":"HomeRoute lifts its cover and stops the 10 s rule only on HomeHost.shown (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart, case 'shown'), which apps/clax_app/home/home.js calls from an effect once its grid, empty state or load error is drawn. A version the agent writes without that call shows the fallback banner every launch although it works. The agent's prompt (apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/) and the kit's fake host (apps/clax_app/assets/kit/fake-home.js, which has no shown member) and its tool text (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart:194) do not mention shown() yet; they should, and the kit's tests could fail a home page that never calls it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"7973fccd63e299579be0c966fa32d22831288f80b6a48393c516be78034af601"},"summary":"A home app version that never calls home.shown() falls back to the built-in home screen 10 s after every load","tags":["home","follow-up","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:54.624351Z","id":"81d5a0ac9bda02b1e28dd9c4dd2e302f9247f0d9c33d2fd7a3ee9a81694b3b4c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the shell posts Ready at the content frame's load event, which can come after the page's first home round trips and its shown(), so a fine page could be timed out and covered by the banner. The rule counts from the route loading the page (first mount, and each reload after Undo or Reset); a later broken version that loads is caught only by 'This app stopped loading'. Would need the shell to tag shown() with the document it came from.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"7973fccd63e299579be0c966fa32d22831288f80b6a48393c516be78034af601"},"summary":"Restarting the 10 s rule at each frame-load ready, so a new version that loads but never draws falls back too","tags":["home","revisit:after the device check of the home app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:10:36.765743Z","id":"11c196d61068b6584b0aab6e74d2a0e17e34d498ee212dbe33cdd386e7f23ad3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The prompts (system.md, single-call.md) tell the agent to call home.shown() once the grid is drawn and never drop it; fake-home.js counts calls in home.shownCount; kit_tool.dart's fake-home.js API text names shown() and how to test it; home/tests/home.test.js 'the shipped page calls shown() exactly once over the kit's fake host'. npx playwright test e2e/home-app.spec.ts: 8 passed (the inspect-view run reports 21 passed); flutter test of home_bundle, home_install, home_update, kit_tool and prompt tests: +54 all passed; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check exits 0.","supersedes":"2be1402a9b0f7fcf0b83be6c7e6b596cb9fec8e4e45adb64b2e15f655cd7f452","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_recovery.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:12:07.618258Z","id":"e3c6105f414d35c108014b15184cb6bb0511172497589296718749349ebd5bea","body":{"detail":"undoLast restores currentVersion - 1 as a new version. Versions v1 (shipped, draws), v2 (broken), v3 (broken, a comment's attempted fix): Undo publishes v4 = v2's files, which falls back after 10 s; Undo again publishes v5 = v3's files; the person alternates between v2 and v3 and only Reset (losing every change) gets out. restoreVersion also keeps the declaration as it is (docs/contract.md:232-248: the title, description, icon and capabilities stay as they are), so a change that dropped or altered a capability, for example `home` itself, is not undone by Undo at all. Options: Undo restores the newest earlier version whose files differ from the current one, or the last version whose page called home.shown() (recorded per content hash by HomeRoute), and puts back that version's capabilities. apps/clax_app/test/home/home_route_test.dart:538-561 covers one Undo only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"67afcfc21bd28a6368c863e22a9ea389421e3735593f2ca9e981c15d70ca870e"},"summary":"Undo last change toggles between the two latest versions: with two broken versions in a row it never reaches the last one that drew, and it keeps the broken version's capabilities","tags":["review","home","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_recovery.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:12:07.618376Z","id":"70815cfe44536cd7b0b4c229039a391558423eb927e6484623e8dbfb90b7b149","body":{"detail":"reset() publishes m.files and records the shipped version in the lineage (home_recovery.dart:98-124), but skips Updater.update's draft run of the bundle's tests and migration (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:283-330). Today home/ has no migrate.js, so nothing breaks yet. Once a shipped release carries one, a Reset from an older release (Keep mine on 1.1.0, then Reset to the 1.1.0 bundle) puts v2 code over v1-shaped documents, and the lineage then says v2, so the migration never runs. Reset could go through Updater.update when the shipped version is above the lineage's, or refuse a bundle with migrate.js.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"6ff2a751cad7e38a63446718c2a25e9d80b6d33a38237c5e70f3e972e8f020b8"},"summary":"Reset publishes the shipped bundle straight over the live documents: no draft check against a copy of the documents and no migrate.js, unlike an update","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:12:07.618549Z","id":"0ce43413eba5da0f3617020b3a98419869454e021cc4c207029e98e109014d87","body":{"detail":"askHomeUpdate shows UpdateSheet, whose Keep mine button reads 'Keep mine (stop updates for this app)' (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart:648). updateHomeApp saves only HomeSettings.keptRelease (home_update.dart:71-74) and never calls Updater.keepMine, so the sheet comes back at the next release, contrary to what the person was told. Either give UpdateSheet a home wording (for example 'Keep mine (skip this update)') or stop updates for real, as the bundle Keep mine does. test/home/home_update_test.dart:137-157 checks the behaviour, not the label.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"45cfd7b5b91d2f334bc0c4b59d50d559ee216558de56272b5aea8e73adf4eec6"},"summary":"The home update sheet's button says \"Keep mine (stop updates for this app)\", but for the home app Keep mine stops only this release's question; the next release asks again","tags":["review","home","copy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:45:28.697346Z","id":"cbfef346bb13b6a45b16fba06bdb35f938bd0ebfb30702d99ab99b20edd83e1c","body":{"detail":"Before Up the snapshot is the whole screen (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _home), so a tap reaches HomeSnapshotView. After Up, HomeRoute stacks the snapshot over the home app's page (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart, the home-snapshot-cover subtree); on macOS AppKit hands a click over a WKWebView to WebKit's view (see record d128991b on apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart), so the click may go to the half-loaded page, not to the cover's GestureDetector. The widget tests (apps/clax_app/test/home/home_snapshot_test.dart) cover only Flutter hit-testing. Unchecked on macOS and Android: the window between Up and shown was about 300 ms on macOS, too short to click by hand.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"270b879cd667ff6cb5da0857bb9940b06a12e11d32480160f949578d31e46306"},"summary":"A tap on the snapshot once the daemon is up may reach the home app's WebView under it instead of the cover","tags":["unverified-on-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:45:28.697384Z","id":"c8cac2b3ff3f4a35b50826aeee54dea9df5be54713d5311655146f499780850a","body":{"detail":"HomeSnapshotView fills SafeArea from the top; AppScreen adds AppScreen.pillStrip to the page's top inset while a build, change or location pill shows (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart, the SafeArea minimum in _page). A snapshot taken then is drawn a strip higher than the page was, and a queued tap maps through rectangles a strip off. The tile rectangles are CSS pixels from the artifact frame's viewport, which on macOS starts at the WebView's top left (checked: the 800x600 snapshot's first tile at x 16, y 64 matched its image).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"270b879cd667ff6cb5da0857bb9940b06a12e11d32480160f949578d31e46306"},"summary":"The snapshot and its tile rectangles are laid out in the full safe area, but the home app's page is inset when its pills strip shows","tags":["home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_recovery.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:46:54.934726Z","id":"297c3ee557742891c26a145a37f3681253cf9a37e0679cb4333900f2a35bb8ec","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e3c6105f414d35c108014b15184cb6bb0511172497589296718749349ebd5bea","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-16): Undo steps back one more version each time.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_recovery.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:47:33.645829Z","id":"64dacd9efb969e19196e6e47b98a36a0da46d58bfef481c0c823a4f0b3d52a26","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: each Undo in a row restores the version before the one the last Undo restored (HomeSettings.undo in home.json). flutter test test/home/home_recovery_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart: All tests passed (35), including 'Undo again steps back one more version, across a restart, until there is none' (v1 good, v2 and v3 broken: two Undos reach v1's index.html, a third says there is no earlier version). Undo still keeps the capabilities as they are; docs/usage.md says so.","supersedes":"e3c6105f414d35c108014b15184cb6bb0511172497589296718749349ebd5bea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:48:42.714640Z","id":"b629b9eeceac5b8b3476113781740177b7335a69cbf0965f542f649840e0f818","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: askHomeUpdate passes keepStopsUpdates: false, so the home sheet's button reads 'Keep mine (skip this update)'; other apps keep 'Keep mine (stop updates for this app)'. flutter test test/home/home_update_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart: All tests passed (39), including 'the home update sheet says Keep mine skips only this update'.","supersedes":"0ce43413eba5da0f3617020b3a98419869454e021cc4c207029e98e109014d87","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:49:53.490473Z","id":"80db1f5a29b5d3f25c633c9337c71959f4070543711dd0127d93e9f41fda78d8","body":{"detail":"home.js useTiles reports on every scroll and resize; HomeSnapshotter.tilesChanged then takes a full capture once reports settle. On Android MainActivity.kt:38-62 runs WebView.draw into a full-resolution ARGB bitmap on the UI thread (software draw of the page; the same thread delivers the WebView's touches under texture-layer composition); on macOS MainFlutterWindow.swift:36-48 encodes a Retina-size PNG in takeSnapshot's completion on the main thread; AppLifecycleState.inactive (app.dart:1206) adds one per focus loss. Each also writes a multi-megabyte file. Options: take the snapshot only when home is covered or backgrounded (the tile list can be saved alone after a scroll), pass a WKSnapshotConfiguration snapshotWidth and downscale the Android bitmap to logical size, and encode off the main thread on macOS.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":248},"end":{"line":256},"content_hash":"62fe548c7d8b6e1255278353a28a1565f6e080ed18a4ab5612a8dee1468bf18d"},"summary":"A snapshot is taken 800 ms after every tile report, including each scroll stop, and both platforms render and encode it on the main thread","tags":["review","performance","unverified-on-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:49:53.490510Z","id":"156a441d8342e8a13c6488dd5e836767b35e65851c0b11c23caeee3cf668ff62","body":{"detail":"Nothing in apps/clax_app/lib calls clear(): choosing 'Use the built-in home screen', Reset and Undo leave home/home-snapshot.bin in the cache directory, and load() never looks at HomeSnapshot.at. The cover is skipped while builtin is on (app.dart _homeCover), but once it is turned off, weeks later, the next cold start shows the old image (names of apps deleted since among it) until shown. The file sits in the app's private cache, so the exposure is to the person themselves. Options: clear on turning builtin on and on Reset, and ignore a snapshot older than a few days.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"97d21b4bf47ea8ddd29947106f3bb95e5a0b66c30c4d5d52b835000de1247775"},"summary":"HomeSnapshotStore.clear has no caller, and a snapshot of any age is shown","tags":["review","home","privacy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:49:53.491323Z","id":"ae483878cde6d3b7c3346425e09e879151842bc5f938aa595394f8a7e42c0af3","body":{"detail":"_lastTiles is set by each home.tiles call and never cleared when the home app's page reloads (a new version, Undo, Reset, a 'stopped loading' reload). The capture in app.dart _watchHome checks only host.tiles != null, so a screen pushed over home, or the app going inactive, while the new page is still blank saves a blank or half-drawn image with the old tile rectangles. On the next cold start a tap on that blank image where a tile used to be opens that app, which the person could not see. Options: clear _lastTiles when the home app's AppScreen starts a load (or when its document changes), or capture only after a shown for the current load.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":369},"end":{"line":374},"content_hash":"d0da3703946a15cb2b9e1a25aede3097f0adf10e97eec0165c5f66a12313a9e2"},"summary":"HomeHost.tiles outlives the page load that reported it, so a capture of a reloading page pairs its image with the previous load's tiles","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:49:53.491430Z","id":"f34ba017d36f83e9c73775c542aa5eb0d96ec6266ea450246ae8b93e4d7da1b5","body":{"detail":"Comment mode is drawn inside the frame (the shell posts clax:comment-mode, web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:319), so it is part of the WebView image. The capture in app.dart _watchHome does not check comment mode, so the person commenting on the home screen (Settings › Home screen › Open) and then switching away, or opening a thread sheet over it, leaves a comment-mode image that the next cold start shows until shown. Flutter routes and sheets over home are not in the image (the platform snapshots only the WebView). Option: skip the capture while the home AppScreen is in comment mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"6f835f120facd3b97df16361b82ff3a338163cc54b447407d0c20fc74f8eb0ac"},"summary":"A snapshot taken in comment mode shows the comment-mode page","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:49:53.491712Z","id":"c183d18051f42c665b4444233e28266e3885341bbbe8b08c903e4a24beb1acde","body":{"detail":"Android: webview_flutter_android uses texture-layer composition (record 1e90d5ce), so touches are hit-tested by Flutter and HomeSnapshotView's opaque GestureDetector takes them; the WebView gets none. macOS: if AppKit hands the click to WKWebView, the cover sees nothing and keeps no tap. Before the page's first render with apps there is no tile under the click, so it is lost, not misrouted. home.js calls shown in the effect right after that render, so a live tile is clickable under the image only for the shown RPC plus one Flutter frame; a click there opens the live tile, which differs from the image only if the grid changed. A double open needs a tap kept before Up and a second click in that same gap. Still unchecked on a device.","kind":"comment","references":"cbfef346bb13b6a45b16fba06bdb35f938bd0ebfb30702d99ab99b20edd83e1c","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"270b879cd667ff6cb5da0857bb9940b06a12e11d32480160f949578d31e46306"},"summary":"Read of the paths: a click goes to one view, so it is either kept by the cover or handled by the page, never both; a wrong app needs the click inside the gap between the page's first render and the cover lifting","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T17:59:17.271788Z","id":"8317ee77c65a5f1e9df533b31f8ef39728e9b2924964ae9df6912100cc49285b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12, f1c07f346b12 and f1c07f346b12: HomeHost.pageLoaded (called at each shell ready of the home page) forgets the tiles and takes reports again only after that load's shown; HomeSnapshotter takes nothing within 500 ms of a load or tile report and drops an image whose HomeHost.renderMark changed while it was taken. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/home -> '+80 ~5: All tests passed!' ('belong to one page load: none before its shown, none after it loads again', 'an image whose render changed while it was taken is dropped, and none is taken just after the page loads or moves').","supersedes":"ae483878cde6d3b7c3346425e09e879151842bc5f938aa595394f8a7e42c0af3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T17:59:17.288202Z","id":"1a9f8401c1e194738567f56d90b9f4ed87d7d7f54669681ebd9bf36d96fb1c78","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: while the snapshot shows and for 300 ms after it lifts, HomeHost.holdActions makes the page's open/openMake/newApp/menu/openInbox/openSettings/importApp do nothing, so a click that reached the WebView under the image opens nothing and only the cover's kept tap can open an app. flutter test test/home/home_snapshot_test.dart -> passes 'do nothing while it shows and just after it lifts, so a tap opens one app at most' (kept tap opens once; page open under the cover and within the grace does nothing; after 300 ms it opens).","supersedes":"cbfef346bb13b6a45b16fba06bdb35f938bd0ebfb30702d99ab99b20edd83e1c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T17:59:17.312712Z","id":"031c16972a3a44f68a474890b8bc5279554f30fd8716dba123512b8b51617e46","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: a tile report only marks the home screen changed; a snapshot is taken 3 s after a load is shown and on a cover or going inactive, each only when home changed since the last. macOS scales to one pixel a point and encodes on a utility queue; Android draws at one pixel a dp. flutter test test/home/home_snapshot_test.dart -> passes 'tile reports alone take none; a shown load takes one once it settles' and 'a cover or the background takes one only when the home screen changed since the last'. macOS release run: 800x600 PNG (was 1600x1200), one snapshot per launch 3 s after shown. Android still unverified on a device (record 3ede332e).","supersedes":"80db1f5a29b5d3f25c633c9337c71959f4070543711dd0127d93e9f41fda78d8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T17:59:17.326541Z","id":"5bb4176316ae9a2cd5d98f65a8f0abb698bd8fdf5581b2d54630221784e8c5ea","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: snapshots record the home app's version; a page of another version drops the cover and clears the kept one; Undo/Reset (HomeRecovery) and choosing the built-in screen (HomeHost) clear it; one older than 7 days is not shown and is cleared. flutter test test/home -> passes 'a snapshot older than a week is not shown, and is cleared', 'a page of another version than the snapshot takes it away and clears it', 'choosing the built-in home screen clears the snapshot', 'a page of another version than the kept snapshot clears it'.","supersedes":"156a441d8342e8a13c6488dd5e836767b35e65851c0b11c23caeee3cf668ff62","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T17:59:17.336151Z","id":"6c4231a7b1179a4c67b256645da10f0737417379113872ae95b868ef71b9aa8d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: no snapshot while the home page's state says comment mode or a composer, or its questions sheet shows; a sheet or dialog pushed over home is no cover. flutter test test/home/app_home_test.dart -> passes 'no snapshot is taken in comment mode, nor when a sheet opens over home; a screen over home takes one', which fails (Expected 0, Actual 1) with the comment-mode and sheet checks removed.","supersedes":"f34ba017d36f83e9c73775c542aa5eb0d96ec6266ea450246ae8b93e4d7da1b5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:34:39.476528Z","id":"81fc70d8be6c188535661b14e3076b856a46922c8838901a9dd6428277e09109","body":{"detail":"_onGallery sets _summaries to [summary, ...?_summaries] while _summaries is still null (load() has not answered), so apps() and the apps event carry just that app. apps/clax_app/home/home.js useLayout (lines 587-591) writes layout/main once, with first: true, as soon as the list is non-empty and nothing is stored, marking only the listed apps seen. When load() answers, every other app is listed but not in seen, so after the update to 1.1.0 they all show the New mark until each is opened. Inputs: no layout/main yet (first start of 1.1.0) and a 'version' gallery event for a non-home app (a build finishing, an import, a sync) arriving before api.listArtifacts() answers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":685},"end":{"line":707},"content_hash":"8e15fc1e46036aa14f0065c31fde6a03c2d1e2704730e3dc43965c4f36cf7cda"},"suggested_fix":"Keep _summaries null (and only remember the event) until the first load answers, or have the home page write its first layout only from a complete list.","summary":"A gallery event before the first app list answers makes apps() a one-app list; the home page's first layout write then marks only that app seen, and every other app reads New","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:44:00.598887Z","id":"1bded0f63cc7df07782cd4d9ad058e6f2a070297da515dbf2af3ef876d44af58","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Gallery events heard before the first listArtifacts() answers are kept in _early and applied to that list, so apps() and the apps event report no apps until it answers. `bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:home_home_host_test`: PASSED, including 'gallery events before the first list answers wait for it: apps() and the apps event never carry a partial list' (failed before the change: Expected empty, Actual one app).","supersedes":"81fc70d8be6c188535661b14e3076b856a46922c8838901a9dd6428277e09109","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:42:15.037598Z","id":"7eca8689ed37f97ad74ae5e22e48e94578bd51b1497574d4879e9842118e5ac8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppScreen no longer insets the page by a pills strip (AppScreen.pillStrip is gone); the page starts at the top inset whatever runs, as the snapshot does. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test passes, including 'the folded chip sits under the top inset…' (page.top == pad.top for status bar 24/48, cutout 56, landscape cutout) and 'the page keeps its place while work starts and ends'.","supersedes":"c8cac2b3ff3f4a35b50826aeee54dea9df5be54713d5311655146f499780850a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_layout.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:53:44.290057Z","id":"a93dc7b7c854c2ced77af2110a02738ebbbd921d2122534e283b5c03b90584ff","body":{"detail":"HomeLayout._change writes layout/main through ClaxApi.batchDocs with if_version set to the version it read, and re-reads and re-applies once on a 409 conflict. The home app's layoutStore (apps/clax_app/home/store.js:60-81) takes a 2 s lease, re-reads, then sets the document last-writer-wins: the page's db has no version to pin. A Flutter star or move that lands after the page's last re-read and before its set is overwritten, and the page's next write (from its reconciled view) does not include it. The window is the page's re-read-to-set gap, as for the unpinned writers b1d1c9e3 (apps/clax_app/home/store.js:60:81) accepts. Closing it needs a version the page can pin (a db set with an if_version), or Flutter taking the page's lease before it writes.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":439},"end":{"line":471},"content_hash":"e629cfdc326c39957ff9ba9d530c07359a3e1aed6135822f03e04b28fb5ebf6c"},"summary":"A page write under its lease (home/store.js:26) can overwrite a pinned Flutter write that landed inside the lease; accepted as b1d1c9e3 accepts the page's own window","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:37:28.651745Z","id":"0fad2b1253a0d777ea3b156a56b03d9b232324d3c61c0d482ccdd7972419a478","body":{"detail":"HomeMake.state is part of the page contract (clax-extensions.d.ts lists making, offline, waiting, interrupted, failed), which has no state for a stopped make; 'interrupted' (Interrupted, replay glyph in home/home.js) is the nearest. The built-in launcher says 'Made a start' (lib/ui/launcher.dart). A 'stopped' state needs a contract version and home.js copy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":686},"end":{"line":695},"content_hash":"94b5207c85366e74aa15783f27e4f6ab9e4de591edc31016721ebdefba961f13"},"summary":"The home app shows a make stopped at a limit as 'interrupted'","tags":["status:needs-decision","contract","make","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_recovery.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:48.828670Z","id":"c76c5872bcb8246e0335444fbe5de43e6931e3e625852676b47660d76d1f7766","body":{"detail":"reset() publishes m.files and records the shipped version in the lineage (home_recovery.dart:98-124), but skips Updater.update's draft run of the bundle's tests and migration (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:283-330). Today home/ has no migrate.js, so nothing breaks yet. Once a shipped release carries one, a Reset from an older release (Keep mine on 1.1.0, then Reset to the 1.1.0 bundle) puts v2 code over v1-shaped documents, and the lineage then says v2, so the migration never runs. Reset could go through Updater.update when the shipped version is above the lineage's, or refuse a bundle with migrate.js.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":97},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"9b8ae49a51e6cb3a420543746ca9268cacd09c11e4413b331026beb08d525262"},"summary":"Reset publishes the shipped bundle straight over the live documents: no draft check against a copy of the documents and no migrate.js, unlike an update","supersedes":"70815cfe44536cd7b0b4c229039a391558423eb927e6484623e8dbfb90b7b149","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T05:35:13.889808Z","id":"9dbd745fe210a74f8356151ad9bd8165a0f62e7f30c5d45b80efca1124d0f143","body":{"detail":"home_install.dart calls Installer.install, which approves the created version's pending capabilities. The shipped bundle is verified against homeInstallKey and checkShipped, but no sheet lists its capabilities. Clax's seeded quickstart is approved by 'clax' itself, not by a person's acceptance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"b16e946f831e8ad391ae2662087c2b4d2ff525f99f1afcf770eba4e028f34303"},"suggested_fix":"Either keep auto-approving as the seeded quickstart is (by 'clax'), or have the home install ask once and approve only on yes.","summary":"The home app's shipped declaration is approved at install without the person seeing it","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_layout.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:03.677894Z","id":"cb32882aa95d7422816cc622ef55969c98a3933c53b6bdf4cb98d64fdfb0971d","body":{"detail":"HomeLayout._change writes layout/main through ClaxApi.batchDocs with if_version set to the version it read, and re-reads and re-applies once on a 409 conflict. The home app's layoutStore (apps/clax_app/home/store.js:60-81) takes a 2 s lease, re-reads, then sets the document last-writer-wins: the page's db has no version to pin. A Flutter star or move that lands after the page's last re-read and before its set is overwritten, and the page's next write (from its reconciled view) does not include it. The window is the page's re-read-to-set gap, as for the unpinned writers b1d1c9e3 (apps/clax_app/home/store.js:60:81) accepts. Closing it needs a version the page can pin (a db set with an if_version), or Flutter taking the page's lease before it writes.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":443},"end":{"line":475},"content_hash":"e629cfdc326c39957ff9ba9d530c07359a3e1aed6135822f03e04b28fb5ebf6c"},"summary":"A page write under its lease (home/store.js:26) can overwrite a pinned Flutter write that landed inside the lease; accepted as b1d1c9e3 accepts the page's own window","supersedes":"a93dc7b7c854c2ced77af2110a02738ebbbd921d2122534e283b5c03b90584ff","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:03.768582Z","id":"825fb8134f979c8f2c6891e03f918c691effdd24aa3e8e7355e49518ead6eae2","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the shell posts Ready at the content frame's load event, which can come after the page's first home round trips and its shown(), so a fine page could be timed out and covered by the banner. The rule counts from the route loading the page (first mount, and each reload after Undo or Reset); a later broken version that loads is caught only by 'This app stopped loading'. Would need the shell to tag shown() with the document it came from.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"7973fccd63e299579be0c966fa32d22831288f80b6a48393c516be78034af601"},"summary":"Restarting the 10 s rule at each frame-load ready, so a new version that loads but never draws falls back too","supersedes":"81d5a0ac9bda02b1e28dd9c4dd2e302f9247f0d9c33d2fd7a3ee9a81694b3b4c","tags":["home","revisit:after the device check of the home app","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:44.335928Z","id":"8955850d5fab995461d25cdb508766e02870d7718ea14902d3947a26da84347d","body":{"detail":"No daemon route serves AppIcons' cached icons under the home app's origin; a data URL needs none and no cross-app read grant. It relies on the artifact CSP leaving img-src open (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs sets none) and grows apps() answers and every apps event by each icon's size.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":657},"end":{"line":677},"content_hash":"8caf9f9835f3abaa64adf6bffeeeae6a603b72a1f0cd058e5ece79520c3d0c0a"},"summary":"apps() gives an app's own icon as a data:image/svg+xml URL of the cleaned SVG, not a daemon-served URL as spec 2026-10-16 section 2 says","supersedes":"a891774fd391ab5ce1b972804caeea6a888e0b7e41bff75143a11b8a5201c67b","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:44.437738Z","id":"4a3c5097edc44f1e84d7fc03a73f8631b5be4b3bfb24ac853da12fc39f2802a7","body":{"detail":"HomeMake.state is part of the page contract (clax-extensions.d.ts lists making, offline, waiting, interrupted, failed), which has no state for a stopped make; 'interrupted' (Interrupted, replay glyph in home/home.js) is the nearest. The built-in launcher says 'Made a start' (lib/ui/launcher.dart). A 'stopped' state needs a contract version and home.js copy.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":685},"end":{"line":694},"content_hash":"26c1e0f20bee88ed7d1ef116a37df2555268a7245eb2f25ae5619fef8c4c0a73"},"summary":"The home app shows a make stopped at a limit as 'interrupted'","supersedes":"0fad2b1253a0d777ea3b156a56b03d9b232324d3c61c0d482ccdd7972419a478","tags":["status:needs-decision","contract","make","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:44.540660Z","id":"022e8a71275a6d27020c8059848c3ebce385c9ed2bf8ca634e50e67cb84d753c","body":{"detail":"ensureHomeApp installs through Installer.install, which writes the lineage entry with role installed and fromBundle: !mine (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:195-204); the home bundle is signed by its release key, never this install's, so mine is false. lib/app.dart passes fromBundleOf(_lineages) to the agent loop. Whether the home app, which the person changes by commenting, should be treated as code from a bundle is for plan Tasks 6 and 7 to settle.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"2e6843992dcad18b3038e8887c25e27fbc257a96e68f119280063d92304274ba"},"summary":"The installed home app is recorded fromBundle: true, so the agent changes it under the bundle isolation rules (fromBundleOf), as any app installed from a file","supersedes":"a47614ec7aae77343e9af4f3d78cdce1e641cd2a7a5a64bfec9c0094d8af5c13","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:44.647969Z","id":"8a1d031cb7c0b408a7f6b87d1e6bd978983154f302bce293f54364632faede52","body":{"detail":"UpdateSheet in its modified form has only Keep mine and Update, but showBundleSheet is dismissible, so a null answer is possible. Asking again on the next start is the chosen reading of 'asks once per release' in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-home-screen-app-design.md section 5; treating a dismissal as Keep mine is the other.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"656c3b5ed8f9cdd8e75dcc6f9e58bb63eaded2713c8d60f5531c92fe2e5391f1"},"summary":"Closing the update sheet without answering (back, or the barrier) returns HomeUpdateResult.none and the same release asks again at the next start; only Keep mine stops the asking","supersedes":"419b2696baf76ee0790f72ce4868a410d4eb193dbec32ef24bca9acaa8c00606","tags":["home-app","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
